We need to implement task 001 correctly. The previous submission failed test "blank project input is rejected": expected alert with role='alert' containing text "Project name is required". Likely the UI didn't create an alert element with appropriate role. Need to implement front-end to show alert visible (maybe <div role="alert">). Also need to ensure blank or whitespace-only name triggers alert and does not add project row.

We must use Node.js 22.22.1, ES modules, built-in http and sqlite. No external dependencies. Use npm start script to run server.

We need to implement server with SQLite DB storing projects (id integer primary key autoincrement, name text). Serve static HTML/JS/CSS. Provide endpoints for creating project (POST /projects), listing projects (GET /api/projects maybe). For simplicity, can embed JS in HTML that uses fetch to backend.

Routing: For root '/', serve index.html with list and creation form.

For /projects/:id, serve project.html showing project name heading and button back to '/'. The server can serve same HTML with dynamic injection using server-side rendering (simple templating) or client fetch.

Simpler: Use client-side JS to fetch project details via API.

Define API endpoints:

- GET /api/projects -> list
- POST /api/projects (JSON {name}) -> create, returns created project {id, name}
- GET /api/projects/:id -> get single

Need to serve /health.

Implementation constraints: No external dependencies, so cannot use express; use node:http.

Also need to serve static files from a directory (public). Use fs to read.

